    "result_text": "The only test class in the project is `AcceptanceTest`, and both of its tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner, following the existing Spring/MapStruct idioms in the codebase.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `OwnerDto` schema (the DTO is code-generated from this spec at build time), documenting the `<TIER>_<AREA>` format and its four possible values.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added an `ownerSegment()` instance method alongside the existing `locality`/`timezone` logic:\n   - **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `effectiveMembershipLevel() >= 3`, else `STANDARD` (reuses the single membership-level resolver).\n   - **AREA** = `METRO` when the owner's locality is a known region (`NSW`, `VIC`, `QLD`), else `REGIONAL`, via a new `KNOWN_REGIONS` set applied to `locality(customerCode)`.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the `@Mapping` entry and a `formatOwnerSegment(owner)` default method delegating to `Owner.ownerSegment()`, mirroring the other derived-field mappers.\n\n**Verification:** `coreSegmentForKnownRegion` (Sydney/NSW + email \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`) and `functionalitySegmentForUnknownRegion` (random city + email \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`) both pass \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
