    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the established pattern in this codebase.\n\n- **Mapper (`formatOwnerSegment`)**: a thin null-guarding delegate to the model, identical in shape to every sibling (`formatMembershipLevel`, `formatLocality`, `formatTimezone`, etc.) and wired into the `@Mapping` block the same way. No logic leaks into the mapper.\n- **Model (`ownerSegment()`)**: the derivation lives on `Owner` alongside the other derived accessors. An instance method is the right unit here because it composes two instance-level derivations (`effectiveMembershipLevel()` and locality from `this.customerCode`), mirroring how `effectiveMembershipLevel()` is itself an instance method \u2014 unlike the pure static `locality`/`timezone` helpers.\n- **`KNOWN_REGIONS` constant**: placed immediately before its sole consumer, matching the existing `CITY_REGION`\u2192`regionForCity` and `REGION_TIMEZONE`\u2192`timezone` convention. Although `REGION_TIMEZONE`'s keyset happens to hold the same three regions, treating \"metro regions\" as a distinct named concept is the right call \u2014 coupling the segment logic to the timezone table's keys would conflate two unrelated meanings.\n- **OpenAPI**: documented consistently with the neighbouring derived read-only fields.\n\nNothing is duplicated, no class is becoming a catch-all, and a maintainer would find this natural.",
